<h1>Evidence &amp; Detection Model</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Signals are evidence with stated provenance and coverage—not declarations that a package is malicious.</p>

<h2>OSV advisory evidence</h2>
<p><code>scan</code> asks OSV whether an exact dependency version falls in a published affected range. <code>confidence: proven</code> means the coordinate matched upstream data deterministically. It does not mean exploitation, reachability, or malicious intent is proven.</p>

<h2>Conditional heuristic stages</h2>
<p>These conceptual groups run only when the ecosystem and available evidence support them:</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Source patterns:</strong> selected JavaScript parsed with vendored Acorn; selected Python checked with patterns. Coverage is bounded.</li>
  <li><strong>Added-dependency metadata:</strong> for an analyzed npm release, profile newly added dependencies for age, sparse metadata, install hooks, same-publisher staging, and name similarity.</li>
  <li><strong>Capability comparison:</strong> compare observable install-hook capabilities only when usable current and previous-version data exists.</li>
  <li><strong>Registry/provenance fields:</strong> inspect publish history, maintainers, repository metadata, and decoded attestation identities. Attestations are not cryptographically verified.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Representative signal names</h2>
<table class="cmd-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Signal</th><th>What it means</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>KNOWN_MALICIOUS</code></td><td>OSV explicitly classified the exact package/version as malicious</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>KNOWN_VULNERABILITY</code></td><td>Exact version matched an ordinary OSV affected range</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>POSTINSTALL_SCRIPT</code></td><td>Consumer install-hook metadata is present</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>MAINTAINER_CHANGE</code></td><td>Observable publishing-account membership changed</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RAPID_PUBLISH</code></td><td>Publish timing crossed the configured heuristic</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>VERSION_ANOMALY</code></td><td>Major jump or dormant-then-active publishing pattern</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>TYPOSQUAT</code></td><td>Name is near a curated popular-package entry under length-dependent edit-distance rules</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>HOMOGLYPH</code></td><td>Invisible, bidirectional, or other non-ASCII characters are present; this is not full confusable mapping</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>CAPABILITY_ESCALATION</code></td><td>A real previous-version comparison shows newly observable dangerous capability</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>INITIAL_DANGEROUS_CAPABILITY</code></td><td>Dangerous capability is present but no usable previous comparison supports an escalation claim</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>AST_DANGEROUS_PATTERN</code> / <code>TARBALL_DANGEROUS_PATTERN</code></td><td>Selected inspectable content matched a risk-associated pattern</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>MISSING_PROVENANCE</code></td><td>No npm provenance attestation was found for a package selected for that stage</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ATTESTATION_IDENTITY_MISMATCH</code></td><td>Decoded subject/source fields disagree with declared package metadata; authenticity is not verified</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Risk scoring</h2>
<p>Scores combine surviving signals and context such as package age, maintainer count, selected allowlist adjustments, and the number of unique signals. Severity is a prioritization mechanism. Context can change it, and configuration can disable documented signals for ordinary reports. Guard ignores those suppressions for its decision.</p>

<h2>CVSS</h2>
<p>Where an advisory supplies a CVSS v3.x vector, vexes calculates a base score using the vector metrics. Missing or malformed upstream severity data may be handled conservatively. This calculation does not turn an advisory into proof that a project is exploitable.</p>

<div class="warning-box"><strong>Coverage is the hard limit.</strong> Typosquat comparison uses a curated list, sampling sees selected files, static patterns miss runtime behavior, and registry/advisory data can lag. The benchmark measures specific cases only.</div>
